# =============================================================================
# What the image builds may see.
#
# There was no .dockerignore, so `docker build .` sent the whole checkout to the
# daemon: every node_modules tree (which `COPY packages/` then laid over the
# ones the image had just installed), the host's dist/ folders, .git, 8 MB of
# research photographs in assets1/, and `.env` — the developer's real
# credentials, one `COPY . .` away from being baked into a layer anybody with
# pull access can read.
#
# The Dockerfiles copy named paths, so nothing below is needed by a build. What
# is listed is what must never reach the build context at all.
# =============================================================================

# Installed and built on the host. The images install and build their own, for
# their own platform; a host copy would replace them with whatever the laptop
# happened to have.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage

# Secrets. Never in a build context, so never in a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and documentation.
.git
docs
specs
DIVE1.md

# Tests ship in no image.
tests
tests3

# Reference material, not product.
assets1

# AI tool folders. Kept in the repository (that is a separate decision) and
# kept out of every image.
.claude
.agents
.specify
.github/agents
.github/prompts

# Local operator output.
backups
_local
.playwright-cli
*.log
